==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|durzanan|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|dʰers-|lang=ine-pro}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''dūra'', Icelandic [[þora]]; (West Frisian [[doare]]), Old High German [[giturran]], Old Saxon [[durran]] and [[gidurran]], Albanian [[nder]] 'honour' and with Greek {{term|θαρσεῖν|lang=grc}}, ‘be bold’.

